==English==

===Alternative forms===
* [[parlor]] {{qualifier|US}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|xno|en}} {{term|parlur|lang=xno}} and Old French {{term|parleor|lang=fro}}, from the verb {{term|parler||to speak}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈpɑːlə/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˈpɑɻləɻ/}}
* {{audio|En-us-parlour.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|ɑː(r)lə(r)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A room for [[talking]], especially the room in a monastery or convent where residents can talk with visitors.
# {{context|dated}} The [[living room]] of a [[house]], or a room for entertaining guests.
# {{archaic}} A [[comfortable]] [[room]] in a [[public house]].
# A [[shop]] or other [[business]] selling goods specified by context.
# A [[shed]] used for [[milking]] [[cattle]].

